    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles so fire and emergency apparatus can reach the residence and detached structure without obstruction.\n• Maintain enough width and overhead clearance along the access drive for a fire truck to pass without stopping to reposition.\n• Keep a turnaround area clear near the residence so apparatus can exit without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Post the property address visibly at the road and again near the residence in case responders enter the property but lose sight of the street marker.\n• Keep the area around the detached structure accessible so responders can reach it without crossing through the landscaped area or open terrain without a clear path.\n• If the perimeter fencing has a gate across the access drive, keep that gate unlocked or install a knox-box so responders are not delayed at the entrance.\n• Identify and mark any secondary foot path or vehicle route around the rear of the property to give responders an alternative if the main driveway becomes blocked."
