    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or touching the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to increase open space between the canopy and the building.\n• Cut back ground vegetation around the base of the structure to reduce the amount of low-growing material close to the walls.\n• Remove or mow dry ground vegetation along both sides of the driveway to reduce the concentration of burnable material along the travel route.\n• Trim tree branches and shrubs that overhang or lean over the driveway surface to keep the full width and height of the route clear for vehicle access.\n• Keep the driveway surface and edges clear of fallen branches, dead leaves, and other debris that could ignite along the access route.\n• Thin shrubs and trees at the driveway entrance to maintain clear sightlines and an unobstructed entry point for vehicles.\n• Separate any shrub groupings near the structure so that plants are not growing in continuous masses that connect directly to the building.\n• Keep the open green space near the structure mowed short to maintain separation between taller surrounding vegetation and the structure.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so that it remains easy to identify quickly from the road, given the single access route to the property."
